  "title": "BGP: Handle Path Identifiers in BGP-MUP NLRI",
  "description": "decode_prefix_MP() skips the 4 octet Path Identifier (RFC 7911) before\ndecoding the NLRI for every SAFI except SAFNUM_BGP_MUP. MUP NLRI\nreceived from a peer that has negotiated ADD-PATH for SAFI 85 are\ntherefore decoded four octets off, which yields bogus Architecture Type\nand Route Type values and a malformed packet for most updates.\n\ndetect_add_path_prefix46() is prefix length based and does not apply to\nthe MUP NLRI layout. The MUP NLRI is self delimiting instead: a one\noctet Architecture Type, a two octet Route Type and a one octet Length.\nWalk the NLRI list both with and without a leading Path Identifier and\nonly assume Additional Path when the walk holds one way and not the\nother, so an NLRI list that already parses without a Path Identifier\nkeeps decoding as before.\n\nAI-Assisted: yes\n\nSigned-off-by: Yuya Kusakabe <yuya.kusakabe@gmail.com>",
